From: Evan Rosner <evanroz@gmail.com>
Sent: Tuesday, January 9, 2024 2:13 PM
To: +WPG725 - CCA RTB <rtb@gov.mb.ca>
Subject: Compliance

Greetings, I received the following email from the Landlord in regards to t=
he storage unit that I have used since the beginning of my tenancy at 10-58=
5 Corydon Ave. "Subject: Storage Lockers. Due to renovations starting in th=
e basement.=E2=80=8A

Greetings,

I received the following email from the Landlord in regards to the storage =
unit that I have used since the beginning of my tenancy at 10-585 Corydon A=
ve.

"Subject: Storage Lockers. Due to renovations starting in the basement. Res=
idents are to have their storage lockers completely emptied by the end of t=
he day on Wednesday, January 17th, 2024. We thank you for your co-operation=
. Sincerely, Thorwin Properties'' (dated Monday January 8,2024)

I have been a tenant at 10-585 Corydon Ave since signing a Standard Residen=
tial Tenancy Agreement with Winpark Dorchester Properties on April 30, 2011=
. I have been using the storage unit located in the basement since the begi=
nning of my tenancy. The storage unit # is correlated with my suite #. I ha=
ve been issued a key that provides access to the storage area as well as th=
e laundry area. All the storage units have been associated with their corre=
lated suites on site. Under the ownership of Winpark Dorchester Properties,=
 each storage unit was labeled with an attached piece of A4 paper that clea=
rly indicated the association between the tenant's suite and storage unit #=
. These labels have since been removed.

Winpark Dorchester Properties sold its property to MyPlace Reality which ha=
s rebranded as Thorwin Properties.

Form 2 (see attached) was not fully completed by Winpark Dorchester Propert=
ies as seen in Section C "Services and Facilities Included in Basic Rent". =
Although water, heat, laundry services, storage facilities, and appliances =
have been provided since the start of the tenancy these boxes have not been=
 checked. This appears to be an oversight and an error on my part for not b=
eing aware that non-completion of Form 2 is a serious issue. There is a rea=
sonable expectation that the services were included in the Standard Residen=
tial Tenancy Agreement with Winpark Dorchester Properties as demonstrated b=
y my continued and uninterrupted use of these services and reiterated in di=
scussion with Celena Funk, Property Manager at Thorwin Properties.

I have communicated with Thorwin Properties about the issue of the storage =
unit (and the laundry services) and proposal for removal since May 4, 2023.=
 As stated by Property Manager Celena Funk on Friday, May 5, 2023, "The Mob=
ile Resident Manager was unaware that your storage locker had been grandfat=
hered in prior to Thorwin Properties purchase of the building. Should at an=
y time we decide to remove the storage units we will apply through the Resi=
dential Tenancy Branch for a withdrawal of service."

Further communications with Thorwin Properties have been ignored until rece=
ntly and since May 4, 2023 I have been requesting that Thorwin Properties f=
ollow legislated protocol.

I feel that it is within my right to continue using the storage unit at 585=
 Corydon Ave and I do not wish to remove my property from the space that I =
have been provided since the beginning of my tenancy. The RTB has not recei=
ved Form 9 (Application to Fix Value of Permanent Reduction or Withdrawal o=
f Service) from Thorwin Properties and I have not received Form 8 (Notice t=
o Tenant =E2=80=93 Permanent Reduction or Withdrawal of Service (Other than=
 a tenant services reduction or withdrawal)).

I would like to request an investigation and I would like to know what the =
consequences of not removing my property from the storage unit on Wednesday=
, January 7, 2024 entails. What response can I expect from the landlord?

Thank you for your time,
Evan Rosner
10-585 Corydon Ave
Winnipeg, MB, Canada
